Subject: [PATCH] Flight Log corpus: AIDev backfill, GH Archive discovery,
 flight pages, claims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The data side of the Flight Logs (scraper brief, 2026-11-02): every public
pull request authored by a coding agent becomes a flight record, the good
ones become indexed pages, and the author can claim them with GitHub sign-in.

- pipeline/: Node 22 package (no build step) — AIDev v3 loader (933k core +
  33.6k pop with computed metrics, events, reviewer excerpts), daily GH
  Archive discovery over BigQuery, batched GraphQL enrichment with rate-limit
  and 5xx handling, deterministic outcome classifier (SQL mirrors TS, parity
  tested), validated LLM debriefs (40-60 words, numbers must match stored
  fields, quotes verbatim from the reviewer excerpt), the index_ok quality
  gate, materialized aggregates, on-brand OG cards, a spot check that blocks
  publish, and a run log per job.
- Supabase Postgres schema (pipeline/migrations/): repos, authors, flights,
  flight_events, claims, pipeline_runs + page RPCs, locked to the service
  role. Riders stay in D1; claims carry the D1 rider id (docs/flight-log-corpus.md).
- Site: /logs/{owner}/{repo}/{number}/, /logs/{owner}/{repo}/, /logs/agent/
  {agent}/ with .json twins, JSON-LD, noindex below the gate, 410 for
  opt-outs and takedowns, corpus sitemaps from Postgres, llms.txt + robots.
- Claim flow: GitHub-sign-in-only proof, claim-all, per-flight visibility,
  the 280-char rider note, rank mirror in D1 (migration 0003) so claimed
  flights count toward the existing thresholds, /me/flights, rider profile
  section, /opt-out, admin takedown + status at /admin/flightlog.
- Scheduled workflows: daily 06:00 discover->enrich->classify->debrief->
  publish, nightly re-enrich + rider cards + rank resync, weekly repo
  refresh, monthly full gate re-run.

Validated end to end on a real AIDev sample (PGlite + wrangler pages dev):
41 pipeline tests, 153 site tests, astro build green.

